The only error-level log increases are in inside-payment (SEVERE "Connection refused" lines) and payment (one error line). The rest of the baseline is unchanged, so I'm treating the payment pod outage as the single root cause.

```json
{
  "root_causes": [
    {
      "service": "ts-payment-service",
      "fault_kind": "pod_failure",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) m, service_name, attr_span_kind k, COUNT(*) n, SUM(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, MIN(attr_http_response_status_code) st, MAX(attr_http_response_status_code) stmax, MIN(time) first_t FROM abnormal_traces WHERE (service_name='ts-payment-service' AND span_name LIKE 'POST%') OR (service_name='ts-inside-payment-service' AND span_name IN ('POST','POST /api/v1/inside_pay_service/inside_payment')) GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "During the 09:25 minute, inside-payment's calls to payment returned 503 (19 of 25 errored) while payment served almost no requests; both recovered by 09:26."
        },
        {
          "kind": "metric",
          "sql": "SELECT time, metric, value FROM abnormal_metrics WHERE attr_k8s_pod_name='ts-payment-service-5ff6f7b6ff-vpt9v' AND metric='container.memory.page_faults' ORDER BY time LIMIT 30",
          "claim": "Payment pod's page-fault counter has a sample gap around 09:25:03-09:25:18 and then drops from about 145k to 28k, consistent with a process restart and recovery."
        },
        {
          "kind": "log",
          "sql": "SELECT time, service_name, level, message FROM abnormal_logs WHERE service_name='ts-inside-payment-service' AND level='SEVERE' ORDER BY time LIMIT 5",
          "claim": "Inside-payment SEVERE logs show 503 upstream failures with 'delayed connect error: Connection refused' when calling payment, all in the 09:25 window."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "propagation": [
    {
      "from": "ts-payment-service",
      "to": "ts-inside-payment-service",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) m, service_name, span_name, attr_span_kind k, COUNT(*) n, SUM(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('ts-inside-payment-service','ts-payment-service') AND span_name LIKE 'POST%' GROUP BY 1,2,3,4 ORDER BY 1,2,3,4",
          "claim": "Inside-payment's POST calls to payment and its own server POST spans both show errors concentrated in the 09:25 minute, while payment's spans were nearly absent."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "from": "ts-inside-payment-service",
      "to": "ts-ui-dashboard",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "kind": "trace",
          "sql": "SELECT date_trunc('minute', time) m, service_name, attr_span_kind k, COUNT(*) n, SUM(CASE WHEN attr_status_code='Error' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END) errs, MIN(attr_http_response_status_code) st, MAX(attr_http_response_status_code) stmax FROM abnormal_traces WHERE service_name IN ('ts-inside-payment-service') AND span_name='POST /api/v1/inside_pay_service/inside_payment' GROUP BY 1,2,3 ORDER BY 1,2,3",
          "claim": "Inside-payment's server POST spans returned 500 for 19 of 25 requests in the 09:25 minute, the calls ui-dashboard routes to it."
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

